urns":4,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I'm approving PKT-0077. The executor did what the goal asked: they ported the cache to the sdkjs source, built and re-measured it, and delivered it as a patch that can be carried. The contract held: the installed files weren't modified and every PDF page came out identical.\n\n**Against the goal**\n- **Source port:** the patch changes only `cell/view/StringRender.js`. It uses the same cache key as PKT-0069 (font name, size, bold/italic, vertical PPI, code points). On a cache hit it writes back the same per-character values the original code writes: grapheme, character index, width and the character itself. Recording happens inside `private_HandleItem`, and `try/finally` clears the recording state if shaping throws. The cache is capped at 200 000 entries. Bold and italic are folded into one value, which is a valid key.\n- **Build and snapshot:** both sides were built from the same sdkjs checkout, and each runs in its own mirror install with a fresh `x2t -create-js-snapshots`. The mirror script deletes the linked `cell/sdk-all.js` and copies a real file in its place, so the installed file is never written through.\n- **Measurement:** the savings are 14–24 %. The executor openly reports that PKT-0069's 26 % on the numbers-only file did not reproduce. All 2 605 pages matched pixel for pixel.\n- **\"Prepare as upstream PR or carried patch\":** it is ready as a carried patch. Opening the PR is left to the follow-up packet, which the goal's \"or\" allows.\n\n**Process checks**\n- **Executor log:** filled in, including surprises and decisions.\n- **Follow-up:** the request is in `.theseus/spawn/PKT-0077-upstream-…font-load.md`. It covers the real risk the executor found: in the browser editor, fonts load lazily, so a cached result shaped with a fallback font could be reused after the real font arrives.\n- **Scoreboard:** the lessons and the friction line are present.\n- **Budget:** 8 files changed against a limit of 6, but only 5 of them are work files; the other three are the packet file, `friction.jsonl` and the spawn request. 257 lines against a limit of 800.\n\n**Weaknesses (not blocking)**\n- `x2t-cpu-ab.py` ignores the x2t return code. A run that crashed would look like a fast run, though the per-run PDF size it prints makes that visible.\n- The page-comparison step (`pdftoppm` plus byte compare) is described but not committed as a script, so the identical-pages result can only be reproduced by following the description.\n- The max memory figure is only an upper bound, because it reads the maximum over all child processes so far (`RUSAGE_CHILDREN`). The report says so. Each timing is a median of only 2 runs.\n- The sdkjs unit tests (QUnit) were not run, and the cache hit rate was not measured. Both are disclosed, and the follow-up packet should cover them before upstreaming.\n\nVERDICT: APPROVE source patch ported faithfully, measured A/B from one build with 2605/2605 identical pages, browser-side font-loading risk handed to a spawned follow-up","ttft_ms":2436,"type":"result","duration_ms":21507,"uuid":"3409ff6f-1808-4376-9b17-b62c0c803557","ttft_stream_ms":952,"time_to_request_ms":336,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":212,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":16,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":21,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":13,"query_setup":3,"auto_mode_context_wait":7,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":24,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":2,"request_build":10},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":45,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":155,"time_to_request_major_faults":63,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":212,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":140,"process_rss_mib_result":226,"process_anon_mib_result":140,"process_pea